{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1040819-so-the-world-of-darkness-and-disease","id":1040819,"title":"So. The World of Darkness and Disease","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-30T12:41:16-08:00","id":1040819,"title":"So. The World of Darkness and Disease","content":"i been thinking about diseases such as Cancer, HIV and so on..i been curious how does the supernatural reacts to it?. it would be easier to develop a supernatural cure to such sickness (not to heal the whole planet for one subject?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T14:09:59-08:00","id":1040884,"title":"","content":"They'd still have to take it seriously, as the capacity to heal such maladies is going to be time-consuming and/or resource intensive, as well as,typically rather rare. Vampires that care about the Masquerade will be particularly concerned with blood-vectored diseases, since they can spread them far and wide with careless feeding practices, and thus leave a fairly wide trail; canonically, there was an HIV flareup investigated by the CDC that started like that in the original Hunter's Hunted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T21:49:45-08:00","id":1041101,"title":"","content":"what about cancer or HIV in the Mage or Werewolves communities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T03:32:49-08:00","id":1041174,"title":"","content":"Read the Prologue of the Syndicate convention book (revised)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T07:57:12-08:00","id":1041253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1040819-so-the-world-of-darkness-and-disease?p=1041101#post1041101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what about cancer or HIV in the Mage or Werewolves communities?</div> </div> </div> </div>The answer to anything and everything in Mage is Magick. They can cure said diseases with Magick.<br /> <br /> Werewolves are immune to (non supernatural) diseases due to their Regeneration. Kinfolk are just as susceptible as normal folk, but there are mystic ways their Garou brethren could go about healing them if it's worth it/necessary (i.e. not something to be done for every kinfolk since it would involve asking/repaying spirits to help).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T08:46:56-08:00","id":1041289,"title":"","content":"I could have sworn one of the Vampire books said Vampires didn't suffer from HIV but could carry and transmit it. It makes sense given the latency period that even they would have a hard time knowing if they were carriers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T09:04:27-08:00","id":1041299,"title":"","content":"I think that they can kill off HIV in their systems if they starve themselves and go into torpor (if there is nothing for the virus to live in, it would die), but I do not remember anything official on that subject. The majority of carriers are not that selfless, however, and are willing to transmit the diseases they carry without regard for basic hygiene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T12:55:57-08:00","id":1041420,"title":"","content":"HIV is relatively fragile outside the living human body, so I imagine altering one's conditions to be as far from that as possible (say, hanging out in a meat locker so that one's internal body temperature was just above freezing for a few hours, or spending the night in a sauna) would do the trick. Smallpox, on the other hand, might be pretty difficult to get rid of...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T14:28:24-08:00","id":1041482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1040819-so-the-world-of-darkness-and-disease#post1040819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i been thinking about diseases such as Cancer, HIV and so on..i been curious how does the supernatural reacts to it?. it would be easier to develop a supernatural cure to such sickness (not to heal the whole planet for one subject?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves and vampires are imune to mundane diseases. Mages can get any of them. But can get better with Life 2 or Entropy 4.<br /> <br /> I also remember seeing vampires being imune to HIV, but being vectors to it. It's somewhere on the second editiion, if I'm not mistaken, I guess.<br /> <br /> For Mages, since it's easy to heal, the problem they may face are diseases caused by Paradox, or created by other supernaturals. Those are harder to deal with.<br /> <br /> But an orphan without life and that have no contact with other Mages, could easily die from a stupid infection without peniciline","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T22:20:41-08:00","id":1041693,"title":"","content":"Ananasi are another exception. They lack the disease immunity of werewolfs but are able to heal diseases by using blood (the amount needed depends on the severity of the disease). Also I'd guess they are as prone to spreading blood-carried diseases as vampires are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T22:58:09-08:00","id":1041702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1040819-so-the-world-of-darkness-and-disease?p=1041693#post1041693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ananasi are another exception. They lack the disease immunity of werewolfs but are able to heal diseases by using blood (the amount needed depends on the severity of the disease). Also I'd guess they are as prone to spreadinge blood-carried diseases as vampires are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh. A bit less prone I would think since their bodies can kill off the disease if they're willing to spend the blood for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T23:21:50-08:00","id":1041711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1040819-so-the-world-of-darkness-and-disease?p=1041702#post1041702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. A bit less prone I would think since their bodies can kill off the disease if they're willing to spend the blood for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, true! As I said they can heal by using blood so probably would only be prone to spreading such a disease while still unaware of it themselves or when doing so intentionally. I think this could be a perfectly fine way of fighting in the mind of some Ananasi.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T02:30:49-08:00","id":1041745,"title":"","content":"I think changellings are also vulnerable huh? That one I'm not sure... Would it be too banal for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T06:56:35-08:00","id":1041795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hexer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1040819-so-the-world-of-darkness-and-disease?p=1041711#post1041711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> well, true! As I said they can heal by using blood so probably would only be prone to spreading such a disease while still unaware of it themselves or when doing so intentionally. I think this could be a perfectly fine way of fighting in the mind of some Ananasi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. It's actually an interesting kill tactic for an Ananasi. And death by disease will probably be blamed on someone else.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1040819-so-the-world-of-darkness-and-disease?p=1041745#post1041745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think changellings are also vulnerable huh? That one I'm not sure... Would it be too banal for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Changelings should be completely vulnerable to diseases. System-wise (currently) none of their Arts directly do anything to cure them.<br /> <br /> Arguably, you could use the right Realm to either command (Sovereign) or Teleport (Wayfare) the disease away though if your ST allows it. Using Changeling Arts can be as much about creativity as Mage Spheres.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T07:11:45-08:00","id":1041805,"title":"","content":"Changeling are vulnerable to disease, but they do have magic, access to the cures of the Dreaming, and access to the Freeholds. The Freehold prevent death by disease and washes away the disease over time (the exact mechanics are vague).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T08:58:58-08:00","id":1041858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1040819-so-the-world-of-darkness-and-disease?p=1041174#post1041174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Read the Prologue of the Syndicate convention book (revised)</div> </div> </div> </div>i dont currently have access to that book. can you sum up please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T10:18:54-08:00","id":1041898,"title":"","content":"Basically, a group of Progenitors &quot;discovered the cure for Cancer&quot; (used Magick to cure cancer), and they were planning to release their 100% effective methods trough mundane agents so it becomes part of the Consensus, but they were suspended by the Syndicate, because the project was deemed too optimistic for the current status quo of the world's population. In other words, the High Ups decided that it was too risky because it could lead to a massive Paradox Backlash if people in general were skeptical to the cure (which they deemed likely).<br /> <br /> Magick can cure everything, but Paradox might not like it, especially if you do this at a big scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T12:08:22-08:00","id":1041947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1040819-so-the-world-of-darkness-and-disease?p=1041420#post1041420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HIV is relatively fragile outside the living human body, so I imagine altering one's conditions to be as far from that as possible (say, hanging out in a meat locker so that one's internal body temperature was just above freezing for a few hours, or spending the night in a sauna) would do the trick. Smallpox, on the other hand, might be pretty difficult to get rid of...</div> </div> </div> </div>I just looked it up, cold doesn't do much to it and it takes temperatures of around 60C to kill it on the high end. Honestly, I think oxygen, alkalinity, and acidity are the most lethal to it so I'm not sure what dropping all vitae would do to change those. It can only survive for only 14 days in decomposing corpses (most likely due to pH changes) but Vampires specifically don't decompose.<br /> <br /> So yeah, a night or two in a dry sauna might do the job. Not entirely sure what that would do to Vampire flesh, but it's unlikely to be anything that couldn't be healed with a few pints.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T18:17:07-08:00","id":1042148,"title":"","content":"Oh, and wraiths, specters and risen are imune too \ud83d\ude01","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T20:20:54-08:00","id":1042203,"title":"","content":"The various supernaturals have ways of dealing with individual illnesses, even as Severe as Cancer. Vampires though likely have the most drawback what with their easiest solution being making you a ghoul or a vampire, unless you are a Methuselah with Obeah/Valeran.<br /> <br /> Werewolves/Fera have the easiest time with this as they have lots of Gifts/Rites/Fetishes/Powers to deal with it, such as a Fetish stick which would allow you to literally beat the AIDS out of someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T21:53:37-08:00","id":1043383,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly, first edition A World of Darkness for Vampire explicitly stated that in certain cases the Black Death could infect vampires and kill them. I believe it was in the section for the UK. So there is precedent for &quot;ordinary&quot; diseases to have some kind of supernatural component to kill things that disease shouldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-03T21:58:26-08:00","id":1043386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1040819-so-the-world-of-darkness-and-disease?p=1043383#post1043383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I remember correctly, first edition A World of Darkness for Vampire explicitly stated that in certain cases the Black Death could infect vampires and kill them. I believe it was in the section for the UK. So there is precedent for &quot;ordinary&quot; diseases to have some kind of supernatural component to kill things that disease shouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div>I usually chalk that up to early edition weirdness. I want to say one of the earlier Vampire books also said there was a strain of AIDS that could kill them as well. Which (obviously) likewise makes little sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}